  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/... \nNear perfect weather is expected for Thanksgiving and through the\nholiday weekend as guidance heavily favors an upper level ridge \nbuilding over the region and staying in place through at least\nSunday. H5 heights are forecast to rise to between 582-585dm \nThursday into Friday before leveling off over the weekend. This \nwould place H5 heights well into the 90th percentile of \nclimatology for late November, while NBM forecast highs rise into \nthe upper 70s across the majority of the lower deserts starting \nThursday. These highs of 5-8 degrees above normal should continue \nthrough the holiday weekend, while lows also warm to a few degrees\nabove normal. Aside from the occasional passing high clouds, \nanticipate mostly clear skies through the period.\n\nModel ensembles then point toward a large Pacific trough setting \nup off the West Coast Sunday into Monday before likely tracking \nthrough our region at some point around next Tuesday and/or \nWednesday. Although still around a week away, models are leaning \ntoward increased precipitation chances by the middle of next week,\nbut so far it does not look like a very strong atmospheric river \nwill impact the Desert Southwest.",
